  "body": "Add the **Mikron WF3 DCM (LinuxCNC)** shipped machine definition from `paulsvc/linuxcnc-mill2-config` (`mill2.ini` and README).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n- Added [assets/machines/mikron-wf3-dcm-linuxcnc.mch](assets/machines/mikron-wf3-dcm-linuxcnc.mch):\n  - 3-axis mill (`vendor: \"Camcraft\"`, `model: \"Mikron WF3 DCM (LinuxCNC)\"`, `kind: \"mill\"`), metric (`mm`, `degrees`).\n  - Program-coordinate travels (`-L..L` per `assets/machines/AGENTS.md`): X `±500 mm`, Y `±500 mm`, Z `±350 mm`.\n  - Axis speeds: X/Z `3000 mm/min`, Y `2100 mm/min` (both normal feed and rapid).\n  - Spindle: `max_speed: 3000.0` rpm, `rigid_tapping: true` (encoder feedback). `min_speed` is omitted rather than `0` (validator requires `> 0`), and `safe_retract` is omitted because `mill2.ini` does not state a machine Z safe retract height.\n  - Coolant: Flood only (`{ \"name\": \"Flood\", \"mCode\": \"M8\" }`).\n  - Tooling: `\"tool_change\": \"manual\"`. `spindle_mount` is omitted because ISO 40 / SK 40 is outside the fixed mount list (`BT30`, `BT40`, `CAT40`, `TTS`), and `number_of_tools` is omitted because there is no tool changer; table size (800x450 mm) and ISO 40 (SK 40) are documented in `general.description`.\n  - Controller post: `\"LinuxCNC\"`.\n- Registered `Mikron WF3 DCM (LinuxCNC)` in `MACHINES` and `embedded` in [crates/app/src/posting_files.rs](crates/app/src/posting_files.rs) and pinned its kind in [crates/app/tests/machine.rs](crates/app/tests/machine.rs).\n- Listed `mikron-wf3-dcm-linuxcnc.mch` in [assets/machines/AGENTS.md](assets/machines/AGENTS.md).\n- Added [crates/app/tests/machine_library.rs](crates/app/tests/machine_library.rs) (`mikron_wf3_dcm_linuxcnc_pins_envelope_spindle_and_refuses_3500_rpm`) to pin the travels, feeds, `3000.0` rpm limit, `rigid_tapping: true`, flood-only coolant, manual tool change, `LinuxCNC` post, and refusal of a `3500` rpm operation.\n- Added [crates/app/tests/linuxcnc_post.rs](crates/app/tests/linuxcnc_post.rs) (`mikron_wf3_dcm_posts_g33_1_rigid_tapping_and_refuses_mist_coolant`) to verify `G33.1` rigid tapping and named refusal of Mist coolant.\n\n### Verification (on `f6b7ad0e5e27a851ece0c3b21bd4930d0ad1a222`)\n- `cargo test -j 10 -p camcraft-app --lib -- posting::files`: 1 passed, 0 failed\n- `cargo test -j 10 -p camcraft-app --test machine_library --test linuxcnc_post --test machine --test posting --test shipped_from_disk`: 81 passed, 0 failed (`linuxcnc_post` 10, `machine` 33, `machine_library` 18, `posting` 17, `shipped_from_disk` 3)\n- `cargo clippy -j 10 -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: pass (exit 0)\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 294 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (35.1 min)\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (18.8 min)\n- `git merge-tree --write-tree upstream/main HEAD`: clean (exit 0)\n\nFixes #3244\nfork synced at v0.26.0\nChangelog: Added the Mikron WF3 DCM (LinuxCNC) shipped machine file with rigid tapping support.\nEffort: medium\n",
